g and drinking in relation to cancers of the oral cavity, pharynx, larynx, and esophagus in northern Italy</article-title><source>Cancer Res</source><year>1990</year><volume>50</volume><fpage>6502</fpage><lpage>6507</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Cancer Res||50|6502||bib10|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2208109</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hsieh</surname><given-names>LL</given-names></name><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>PF</given-names></name><name><surname>Chen</surname><given-names>IH</given-names></name><name><surname>Liao</surname><given-names>CT</given-names></name><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>HM</given-names></name><name><surname>Chen</surname><given-names>MC</given-names></name><name><surname>Chang</surname><given-names>JTC</given-names></name><name><surname>Cheng</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Characteristics of mutations in the p53 genes in oral squamous cell carcinoma associated with betel quid chewing and cigarette smoking in Taiwanese</article-title><source>Carcinogenesis</source><year>2001</year><volume>22</volume><fpage>1497</fpage><lpage>1503</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Carcinogenesis||22|1497||bib11|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11532872</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Johnson</surname><given-names>NW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A global view of the epidemiology of oral cancer</article-title><source>Oral Cancer: Detection of Patients and Lesions at Risk</source><year>1991</year><publisher-name>Cambridge: Cambridge University Press</publisher-name><fpage>3</fpage><lpage>26</lpage>Johnson NW (ed) pp</citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Klijn</surname><given-names>JG</given-n